{"name":"Ekurhuleni","slug":"ekurhuleni","region":"Africa","lat":-26.2,"lon":28.25,"seasons":{"DJF":{"season_name":"Dec 2026–Feb 2027","years":[1951,1952,1953,1954,1955,1956,1957,1958,1959,1960,1961,1962,1963,1964,1965,1966,1967,1968,1969,1970,1971,1972,1973,1974,1975,1976,1977,1978,1979,1980,1981,1982,1983,1984,1985,1986,1987,1988,1989,1990,1991,1992,1993,1994,1995,1996,1997,1998,1999,2000,2001,2002,2003,2004,2005,2006,2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024,2025],"roni_lead":[-0.38,0.98,0.04,0.84,-0.31,-1.31,-0.14,1.16,0.24,0.04,0.08,-0.16,-0.3,1.06,-0.64,1.86,-0.03,-0.08,0.56,0.67,-0.57,-0.4,1.82,-1.63,-0.45,-0.95,1.04,0.89,-0.08,0.52,-0.06,-0.17,2.03,-0.9,-0.61,-0.18,1.0,1.2,-1.71,-0.23,0.27,1.2,0.1,0.46,0.97,-0.93,-0.25,2.22,-1.33,-1.06,-0.55,-0.18,1.18,0.17,0.7,-0.18,0.73,-1.33,-0.38,0.86,-1.61,-0.91,0.21,-0.22,0.35,2.03,-0.96,-0.82,0.62,0.15,-1.37,-1.08,-1.1,1.3,-0.76],"paragraph":"Dec–Feb in Ekurhuleni has warmed by about 0.2 °C per decade since 1951, roughly 1.5 °C in all. There is a strong, well-established El Niño effect on temperature: after El Niño conditions in the preceding Sep–Nov, Dec–Feb tends to run warmer, and El Niño accounts for about 45% of the year-to-year ups and downs. With this year's strong El Niño, that push is about 2 times a normal year-to-year swing, roughly as much warmth as 55 years of the long-term trend. Without El Niño, a Dec–Feb this warm would come about once every 54 years. El Niño moves the hottest days most: this season they are expected to shift by about 1.6 °C, against 0.8 °C for the coldest days. Dec–Feb rainfall shows no clear long-term trend, but El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a drier season with fewer rainy days and less intense heavy-rain days, and this year's shift is substantial. Relative humidity has fallen by about 0.5 points per decade, roughly 3 points since 1951; because warmer air holds more moisture, this does not necessarily mean the air is drier. El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a less humid Dec–Feb, and this year's shift is larger than a normal year-to-year swing. For Dec 2026–Feb 2027, a warmer-than-normal season is very likely (more than 95% chance), about 1.6 °C above the 1991–2020 average; a drier-than-normal season is more likely than not (about 60%), and a less humid season than normal is likely (about 75% chance). This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":19.9922,"trend_per_decade":0.2015,"trend_p":0.0,"trend_total_since_1951":1.5113,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.5072,"enso_p":0.0,"confidence":"Strong","survives_fdr":true,"fraction_explained":0.4417,"intrinsic_sd":0.5345,"effect_this_season":1.1159,"effect_ratio":2.0878,"size":"Dominant","size_typical_el_nino":"Dominant","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":54.0,"expected_anomaly_2027":1.5799,"p_below":0.0009,"p_near":0.0098,"p_above":0.9893,"forecast_words":"Very likely (>95%): a warmer-than-normal season","within_record":true,"years_of_warming_equivalent":55.375,"values":[19.607,20.095,19.391,20.056,18.082,18.193,18.537,19.47,18.956,18.849,19.308,19.724,19.027,20.094,18.994,20.272,19.083,19.406,20.806,19.234,18.924,19.213,20.791,18.674,18.515,17.939,19.533,19.257,19.669,18.97,19.285,19.611,20.967,19.847,20.155,19.525,20.199,20.464,18.21,18.974,20.058,20.514,20.368,18.933,20.017,18.574,19.654,19.846,19.542,18.581,19.317,19.329,19.959,20.445,19.795,19.596,21.054,19.248,20.056,20.178,19.497,20.358,20.217,20.387,20.575,22.127,20.19,20.236,21.047,20.069,20.239,19.3,19.817,20.753,21.135],"forecast_mean":21.5721,"forecast_sd":0.5862,"fit":{"a2027":20.4562,"b":0.5072,"c":0.0202,"tercile_low":19.7478,"tercile_high":20.2232},"percentiles":{"p05":{"trend_per_decade":0.1573,"trend_p":0.0,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.367,"enso_p":0.0007,"confidence":"Strong","shift_this_season":0.8073,"lines_cross":false}