 strong El Niño, that push is about as large as a normal year-to-year swing, roughly as much warmth as 42 years of the long-term trend. Without El Niño, a Mar–May this warm would come about once every 8 years. Mar–May rainfall shows no clear long-term trend, but El Niño has a modest but consistent effect toward a drier season, and this year's shift is a noticeable tilt. Humidity shows no clear long-term trend, but El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a less humid Mar–May, and this year's shift is substantial. For Mar–May 2027, a warmer-than-normal season is likely (about 85% chance), about 1.3 °C above the 1991–2020 average; a less humid season than normal is likely (about 70% chance). This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":15.5893,"trend_per_decade":0.1951,"trend_p":0.0,"trend_total_since_1951":1.4632,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.3762,"enso_p":0.0001,"confidence":"Strong","survives_fdr":true,"fraction_explained":0.1849,"intrinsic_sd":0.7402,"effect_this_season":0.8275,"effect_ratio":1.1179,"size":"Dominant","size_typical_el_nino":"Substantial","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":8.0,"expected_anomaly_2027":1.3351,"p_below":0.0194,"p_near":0.1317,"p_above":0.8489,"forecast_words":"Likely (85%): a warmer-than-normal season","within_record":true,"years_of_warming_equivalent":42.418,"values":[15.079,14.871,15.249,16.689,13.776,15.43,15.056,15.803,15.344,14.049,15.366,15.108,14.396,15.768,15.069,15.069,14.198,13.606,14.748,15.867,15.411,14.37,15.215,13.933,14.038,14.112,14.559,14.553,16.087,15.08,14.624,14.767,16.2,15.557,15.295,16.233,16.862,15.483,14.907,14.765,15.166,16.33,15.469,15.26,14.99,14.361,13.458,16.487,16.333,14.256,15.427,15.89,16.578,15.282,15.254,13.781,16.316,14.573,15.199,16.094,15.581,15.913,15.618,15.49,16.952,16.852,16.115,16.238,17.053,15.364,16.338,15.201,16.363,17.694,15.555],"forecast_mean":16.9